<div class="header-box">
  <h1>CIVICMIND AI</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">"Predict • Prioritize • Prevent" — Technical Architecture, Implementation, and Prototype Report</div>
  <p><strong>System Name:</strong> CivicMind AI — Full-Stack Municipal Grievance Redressal & Spatial Intelligence Platform<br>
  <strong>Target Application:</strong> Municipal Grievance Tracking, AI Triage, and Spatial Hotspot Detection<br>
  <strong>Stack:</strong> React 18 (Vite), Python 3.12 (FastAPI), Scikit-Learn (TF-IDF & DBSCAN), SQLite (SQLAlchemy 2.0)</p>
</div>

<h2>1. Technical Architecture and Design</h2>

<h3>1.1 Architecture Overview</h3>
<p>CivicMind AI is implemented as a decoupled, asynchronous <strong>Full-Stack Web Application</strong>. The frontend is a client-side Single Page Application (SPA) communicating over RESTful HTTP APIs with an asynchronous FastAPI backend engine, underpinned by local SQLite relational storage and an embedded Machine Learning inference subsystem.</p>

<pre>
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                           FRONTEND CLIENT (Port 5173)                             |
|         React 18 SPA (Vite + Tailwind CSS + React-Leaflet + Lucide Icons)         |
|  ┌─────────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐  ┌───────────────────────────┐  |
|  |  Citizen Dashboard  |  |  Manager Dashboard  |  |   Admin Master Dashboard  |  |
|  └─────────────────────┘  └─────────────────────┘  └───────────────────────────┘  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                         │  ▲
                     HTTP / REST API via Axios  │  JWT Bearer Token
                                         ▼  │
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                            BACKEND API (Port 8000)                                |
|                       FastAPI Asynchronous Web Engine                             |
|  ┌─────────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐  ┌───────────────────────────┐  |
|  |   /api/auth/        |  |  /api/complaints/   |  |      /api/dashboard/      |  |
|  └─────────────────────┘  └─────────────────────┘  └───────────────────────────┘  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                  │                                                 │
                  ▼                                                 ▼
+------------------------------------+            +---------------------------------+
|       EMBEDDED AI / ML PIPELINE    |            |       PERSISTENCE LAYER         |
|  - NLP Classifier (TF-IDF + Bayes) |            |  SQLite Database (civic_app.db) |
|  - Hotspot Clustering (DBSCAN)     |            |  SQLAlchemy 2.0 ORM             |
+------------------------------------+            +---------------------------------+
</pre>

<h3>1.2 Implemented Database Schema (backend/models.py)</h3>
<p>The system stores all state in a localized SQLite database (<code>civic_app.db</code>) managed by SQLAlchemy ORM with four primary entities:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Table Name</th>
      <th>Primary Columns</th>
      <th>Relationships & Key Constraints</th>
      <th>Functional Role</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>users</strong></td>
      <td><code>id, name, first_name, last_name, contact_number, occupation, email, password_hash, role, department_id</code></td>
      <td>Primary Key: <code>id</code><br>Unique: <code>email</code><br>Foreign Key: <code>department_id</code></td>
      <td>Stores citizen credentials, full profile details, and role privileges (CITIZEN, OFFICER, ADMIN).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>departments</strong></td>
      <td><code>id, name</code></td>
      <td>Primary Key: <code>id</code><br>Unique: <code>name</code></td>
      <td>Municipal departments (Roads, Electricity, Water & Sanitation, Waste Management).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>complaints</strong></td>
      <td><code>id, citizen_id, description, address, image_url, latitude, longitude, department_id, status, created_at</code></td>
      <td>Foreign Keys:<br>• <code>citizen_id → users.id</code><br>• <code>department_id → departments.id</code></td>
      <td>Contains issue text, reverse geocoded address, Base64 photo proof, GPS coordinates, and status.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>hotspots</strong></td>
      <td><code>id, center_latitude, center_longitude, complaint_count, severity, created_at</code></td>
      <td>Primary Key: <code>id</code></td>
      <td>Maintains active DBSCAN spatial clusters calculated from unresolved complaints.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>1.3 Authentication & Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Password Security:</strong> Passwords are encrypted before database insertion using <code>bcrypt</code> with salting via Python's <code>passlib</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Cryptographic Tokens:</strong> User sessions issue signed <code>JSON Web Tokens (JWT)</code> using the <code>HS256</code> algorithm and a 24-hour expiration payload containing user ID, email, and role.</li>
  <li><strong>Axios Interceptor:</strong> The frontend HTTP client (<code>frontend/src/api.js</code>) dynamically attaches the Bearer token to the <code>Authorization</code> header for authenticated requests.</li>
  <li><strong>Access Boundaries:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Citizen:</strong> Restricted strictly to reporting issues and fetching their own personal submissions (<code>/api/complaints/my</code>).</li>
      <li><strong>Officer (Manager):</strong> Authorized to access the city-wide complaint list, view citizen contact cards, update resolution statuses, and launch Google Maps routing.</li>
      <li><strong>Admin:</strong> Authorized to access the Master Database, modify user roles, delete complaints, and inspect the DBSCAN AI Heatmap.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Implementation and Prototype Development</h2>

<h3>2.1 Frontend User Interface & Dashboards</h3>

<h4>A. Authentication Portal (frontend/src/App.jsx)</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Dual-Tab Layout:</strong> Integrated toggle between <strong>Sign In</strong> and <strong>Create Account</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Citizen Profiling:</strong> Captures First Name, Last Name, Contact Number, Email, Password, and Occupation (Local Resident, Student, IT Professional, Healthcare Worker, Government Employee, Civil Engineer, etc.).</li>
  <li><strong>Instant Session Initiation:</strong> Automatically signs in and redirects the citizen to their dashboard upon successful registration without requiring a second login.</li>
  <li><strong>Interactive Controls:</strong> Password visibility toggle using Lucide React icons (<code>Eye</code>, <code>EyeOff</code>) and minimum 6-character client validation.</li>
</ul>

<h4>B. Citizen Dashboard (frontend/src/pages/CitizenDashboard.jsx)</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Interactive GIS Map:</strong> Powered by <code>react-leaflet</code>, centered on the geographic center of India (<code>[20.5937, 78.9629]</code>) at zoom level 5.</li>
  <li><strong>HTML5 Geolocation:</strong> <code>📍 Detect My Location</code> triggers browser GPS coordinates and animates the map to street level.</li>
  <li><strong>Reverse Geocoding:</strong> Automatically queries the OpenStreetMap Nominatim API to translate latitude/longitude into a real street address.</li>
  <li><strong>Center India Shortcut:</strong> Provides an <code>🇮🇳 Center India</code> button that immediately resets the map view to the country overview.</li>
  <li><strong>In-Browser WebRTC Camera:</strong> Streams the user's camera via <code>navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia</code>, renders to an HTML5 Canvas, and extracts a Base64 image directly inside the browser.</li>
  <li><strong>Form Validation:</strong> The submission button is disabled with gray styling until at least 10 description characters and a map location are selected.</li>
  <li><strong>Isolated "My History" View:</strong> Queries <code>/api/complaints/my</code> to ensure citizens exclusively see complaints submitted from their account. Expandable accordion rows display full descriptions, addresses, timestamps, status badges, and attached photos.</li>
</ul>

<h4>C. Manager Dashboard (frontend/src/pages/OfficerDashboard.jsx)</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>City Queue:</strong> Displays all complaints submitted across the city in an expandable table.</li>
  <li><strong>Citizen Contact Card:</strong> Expanding an issue reveals the reporter's full name, occupation, a one-click <code>📞 Call</code> dialer button (<code>tel:</code>), and an email launcher (<code>mailto:</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Google Maps Navigation:</strong> Provides dynamic links (<code>https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination={lat},{lng}</code>) allowing field staff to launch turn-by-turn navigation directly to the incident.</li>
  <li><strong>Live Resolution Workflow:</strong> Dropdown enables status updating from <code>Pending</code> to <code>In Progress</code> or <code>Resolved</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h4>D. Admin Master Control Panel (frontend/src/pages/AdminDashboard.jsx)</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>System Metrics:</strong> Counters tracking Total Users, Managers, Total Complaints, and Active Hotspots.</li>
  <li><strong>AI Hotspot Heatmap:</strong> Leaflet map plotting active DBSCAN clusters as interactive <code>CircleMarker</code> elements (Red = High severity, Yellow/Orange = Medium severity) with issue count popups.</li>
  <li><strong>Categorized User Management:</strong> Separates City Managers from general Citizens. Admins can promote/demote user roles or delete accounts.</li>
  <li><strong>Master Database & Pagination:</strong> Displays all records with override and purge controls, paginated to 10 rows per page to safeguard browser rendering.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2.2 Implemented AI & Machine Learning Subsystems</h3>

<h4>A. Natural Language Processing Department Classifier (backend/ai/nlp_classifier.py)</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Algorithm:</strong> <code>TfidfVectorizer</code> (term frequency-inverse document frequency) combined with a <code>MultinomialNB</code> (Multinomial Naive Bayes) pipeline.</li>
  <li><strong>Automated Routing:</strong> Automatically classifies complaint text into municipal departments:
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Roads:</strong> potholes, cracked asphalt, road hazards.</li>
      <li><strong>Electricity:</strong> broken street lights, blackouts, damaged power lines.</li>
      <li><strong>Water & Sanitation:</strong> water pipe burst, drainage overflowing, sewage.</li>
      <li><strong>Waste Management:</strong> uncollected garbage, overflowing dumpsters.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Persistence:</strong> Automatically trains and saves the model to <code>nlp_model.pkl</code> on first launch if not already cached.</li>
</ul>

<h4>B. Spatial Density Clustering for Hotspot Detection (backend/ai/hotspot_detector.py)</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Algorithm:</strong> Scikit-Learn <code>DBSCAN</code> with radius $\varepsilon = 0.005$ ($\approx 500\text{ meters}$) and $\text{min\_samples} = 3$.</li>
  <li><strong>Unresolved Focus:</strong> Clusters strictly complaints where <code>status != 'Resolved'</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Centroid Calculation:</strong> Calculates arithmetic mean latitude and longitude of clustered complaints.</li>
  <li><strong>Severity Assessment:</strong> Categorized as <strong>High</strong> severity if cluster contains $\ge 5$ complaints, otherwise <strong>Medium</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Real-Time Eviction:</strong> Whenever a complaint is marked <code>Resolved</code> by a manager or deleted by an admin, <code>detect_hotspots()</code> recalculates clusters; if unresolved issues in a cluster fall below 3, the hotspot is automatically evicted from the database in real-time.</li>
</ul>

