<h3>3.2 Testing Scenarios Conducted</h3>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Authentication & Role Routing:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Verified login with all three pre-seeded accounts: Citizen (<code>alice@test.com</code>), Manager (<code>manager@city.com</code>), and Admin (<code>admin@city.com</code>).</li>
      <li>Validated that unauthorized roles cannot view the Admin dashboard (displays an Administrator Access Required security screen).</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Citizen Data Isolation:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Logged in as Alice and submitted issues. Registered a second citizen account and verified that the second user's "My History" starts completely blank (<code>0 Filed by you</code>).</li>
      <li>Confirmed that <code>/api/complaints/my</code> filters strictly by <code>Complaint.citizen_id == current_user.id</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Hotspot Lifecycle & Eviction:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Submitted 3 complaints within a 300-meter radius. Verified that the Admin Heatmap renders an active hotspot circle.</li>
      <li>Updated 1 complaint to <code>Resolved</code> via Manager Dashboard. Verified that the active hotspot circle is immediately purged from the database and disappears from the heatmap.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Hardware & Geolocation APIs:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Verified that the HTML5 WebRTC camera opens, takes snapshot captures, and converts them to valid Base64 image URIs stored in SQLite.</li>
      <li>Verified that <code>📍 Detect My Location</code> accurately retrieves browser coordinates and reverse geocodes them into human-readable street names.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>

<h3>3.3 Performance Validations Implemented</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Asynchronous Toast Notifications:</strong> Replaced blocking browser <code>alert()</code> dialogs with a non-blocking Toast system (<code>ToastContext.jsx</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Concurrent Submission Guards:</strong> Form buttons disable and show animated <code>Loader2</code> spinning icons while awaiting server responses, preventing duplicate submissions.</li>
  <li><strong>Safe Startup Auto-Migrations:</strong> Backend startup checks execute safe <code>ALTER TABLE</code> SQL statements for new columns (<code>address</code>, <code>first_name</code>, <code>last_name</code>, <code>contact_number</code>, <code>occupation</code>) so existing SQLite databases never fail on startup.</li>
  <li><strong>DOM Throttling via Pagination:</strong> The Admin Master Database displays complaints in slices of 10 to ensure steady browser rendering performance.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Industry Readiness and Refinement</h2>

<p>This section details the specific engineering standards and code quality refinements <strong>already present in the current codebase</strong>:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Modularity & Separation of Concerns:</strong> The codebase is structured into isolated layers: API routers (<code>routes/</code>), Machine Learning logic (<code>ai/</code>), database schema (<code>models.py</code>), and role-specific UI views (<code>pages/</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Data Sanitization & Circular Reference Prevention:</strong> The backend cleans model outputs into explicit dictionaries, detaching circular ORM relationships and excluding password hashes before JSON transmission.</li>
  <li><strong>Dual User Lookup in Authentication:</strong> The <code>get_current_user</code> dependency looks up users by both primary key ID and email claim, ensuring session continuity regardless of token age.</li>
  <li><strong>Local Windows Scripts:</strong> The repository includes complete startup automation scripts:
    <ul>
      <li><code>requirements.txt</code>: Complete Python dependency manifest.</li>
      <li><code>seed.py</code>: One-step database seeding script.</li>
      <li><code>start_backend.ps1</code>: Virtual environment activation and FastAPI server launch.</li>
      <li><code>start_frontend.ps1</code>: Vite frontend launcher.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Repository Cleanliness:</strong> Configured <code>.gitignore</code> strictly excluding temporary directories (<code>node_modules/</code>, <code>backend/venv/</code>, SQLite database binaries, and Python cache).</li>
</ul>

